    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for today is headlined by **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who stand as our most reliable assets despite challenging matchups against elite arms. **Jackson Merrill** leads the pack with a 50.99 score, buoyed significantly by a +13% dynamic platoon adjustment against Misiorowski. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** manages a 51.04 score; while he faces a formidable arm in Rasmussen, the algorithm rewards his presence in the #3 spot and the significant boost from his platoon advantage. **Kyle Tucker** remains a high-floor start at 51.97, maintaining his efficiency even against Dodd, as the raw talent level of the veteran helps insulate his scoring potential despite a neutral park environment.\n\nWe find ourselves navigating a difficult slate of opposing pitchers, with nearly every starter facing an xERA below 3.60. **Drake Baldwin** earns a start at 47.11 primarily due to the leadoff volume he provides, which is critical for our run-scoring potential. **Miguel Vargas** also earns the nod at 47.23, supported by a strong 0.378 xwOBA metric that helps him overcome the SP skill penalty posed by Messick. The most difficult personnel decision today involved **Brayan Rocchio**, who landed at 34.60. While his dynamic platoon edge provided a marginal lift, his lower spot in the order coupled with the 3.07 xERA of the opposing pitcher failed to clear the 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" Consequently, **Brayan Rocchio** stays on the bench to preserve our game caps, as we prioritize the higher-ceiling roles of **Liam Hicks** and **Andy Pages** despite their own SP-related scoring suppression. We remain on high alert for weather developments, though current projections suggest no immediate risks to our starters.",
